### /refactor
- MUST FOLLOW the style of the classes contained in the `fact_extractor.py` for all modules in src/.
- You are working inside a production codebase. 

#### IMPORTANT RULES FOR PRODUCTION CODE BASES 

- Apply DRY (Don't repeat yourself) principles.
- Apply software engineering best practices KISS (Keep it simple stupid).
- Apply software engineering best practices SOLID (Single responsibility principle, Open Closed principle, Liskov substitution principle, Interface segregation principle and Dependency inversion principles).
- Refactor every piece of code for clarity and maintainability.
- Minimal diff.
- No new abstractions.
- No behavior change unless it is a bug, then fix it.
- Create documentation for each function.
- Prefer clarity.
- Prefer early returns.
- Ask before large refactors.
- Ask clarifying questions if you are unsure.
